# data-models-relationships

Core Data Models:

1. Inmate Records
- Bond status tracking
- Compliance history
- Photo verification records
- Location check-in logs

2. Bond Records
- Compliance requirements
- Geographic boundaries
- Verification schedules
- Status transitions

3. Agent Profiles
- County assignments
- Office hour availability 
- Call routing preferences
- Case load tracking

4. Location Records
- GPS coordinates
- Accuracy radius
- Verification timestamps
- VPN/proxy detection flags

Key Relationships:

1. Inmate → Bond Records
- One-to-many relationship
- Active bond tracking
- Historical bond archive
- Compliance status linkage

2. Inmate → Location Records
- One-to-many relationship
- Check-in history
- Compliance verification points
- Geographic boundary violations

3. Agent → Cases
- Many-to-many relationship
- Case assignment tracking
- Office jurisdiction mapping
- Coverage scheduling

4. Bond → Verification Events
- One-to-many relationship
- Photo verification entries
- GPS check-in records
- Compliance refusals

Schema Highlights:

```python
# Simplified core schema relationships
Inmate:
  - active_bonds
  - location_history
  - verification_photos
  - compliance_status

Bond:
  - assigned_inmates
  - geo_boundaries
  - verification_schedule
  - compliance_rules

Agent:
  - assigned_cases
  - office_location
  - availability_hours
  - routing_preferences

Location:
  - gps_coordinates
  - verification_status
  - compliance_flags
  - accuracy_metrics
```

